        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.limics.fr/ontologies/ontoparonnoy#MetaObjetAbstrait"/>
        <ontoparonnoy:UMLS_id>C0449234</ontoparonnoy:UMLS_id>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Un travail doit être mené pour vérifier les différents élements des attributs.
Une coordonée est elle un atribut génerique ou bien un &quot;attribut social??&quot;</rdfs:comment>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">As a concept in the CG sense, an attribute a unary relation, Its logical interpretation, i.e. its denotation, consists of every occurrence of the attribute for what it is an attribute of: e.g. denotation of temperature is the set of temperature of every patient at every time.  The graph of the attr relation will be, regarding temperature,  {(#123, T(t1, #123))...} An attribute characterises a property intrinsic of an object. It is a point of view that is internalised in the object definition. This must be constrasted to with the functional point of view that are external considerations to the object that are not necessarily considered in the object definition.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">attribut</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">attribute</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


